  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Justice obligated $7.4B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Justice awarded 43,342 contracts during the same period with an average award size of $170K. Obligations fell 13.4% year over year. Annual obligations peaked at $10B in FY23 and then moved to $9.4B in FY24, $8.5B in FY25, and $7.4B in FY26. The Department of Justice spent $871M on Other Computer Related Services and $758M on Security Guards and Patrol Services so far in FY2026. The Department of Justice also obligated $682M to General Medical and Surgical Hospitals and $488M to Other Residential Care Facilities in the current fiscal year to date. METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. received $515M, NAPHCARE LLC received $204M, and MCKESSON CORPORATION received $168M in FY2026 to date. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Justice's contract obligations changed over recent years?",
        "body": "The Department of Justice obligated $9.1B in FY21, $9B in FY22, $10B in FY23, $9.4B in FY24, $8.5B in FY25, and $7.4B in FY26. Obligations fell 13.4% year over year into FY26. The Department of Justice awarded 43,342 contracts in FY2026 to date, with an average award size of $170K. The Department of Justice's FY2026 total is a partial fiscal year figure and reflects year-to-date spending."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Justice's largest purchase categories and top suppliers in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the largest category at $871M, followed by Security Guards and Patrol Services at $758M and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $682M. Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $442M and Custom Computer Programming Services accounted for $277M in FY2026 to date. METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. is the top vendor at $515M, followed by NAPHCARE LLC at $204M and MCKESSON CORPORATION at $168M. The Department of Justice also obligated $154M to AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC and $145M to THE GEO GROUP, INC."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Justice spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Justice obligated $7.4B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Justice awarded 43,342 contracts in the period with an average award size of $170K. Obligations fell 13.4% year over year and FY2026 totals are partial fiscal year to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Justice buy?",
      "a": "Justice buys services and facilities support across technology, security, and healthcare. Other Computer Related Services received $871M, Security Guards and Patrol Services received $758M, and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals received $682M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Justice also obligated $488M to Other Residential Care Facilities, $442M to Computer Systems Design Services, and $277M to Custom Computer Programming Services."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Justice's largest contractors?",
      "a": "METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. is Justice's largest contractor at $515M. NAPHCARE LLC is the second largest at $204M and MCKESSON CORPORATION is the third largest at $168M. Additional top vendors include AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC at $154M, THE GEO GROUP, INC. at $145M, and CGI FEDERAL INC. at $139M."
